{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1536","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Omkar and Medians"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Uh oh! Ray lost his array yet again! However, Omkar might be able to help because he thinks he has found the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OmkArray"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of Ray's array. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OmkArray"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of an array $$$a$$$ with elements $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{2k-1}$$$, is the array $$$b$$$ with elements $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_{k}$$$ such that $$$b_i$$$ is equal to the median of $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{2i-1}$$$ for all $$$i$$$. Omkar has found an array $$$b$$$ of size $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$-10^9 \\leq b_i \\leq 10^9$$$). Given this array $$$b$$$, Ray wants to test Omkar's claim and see if $$$b$$$ actually is an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OmkArray"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of some array $$$a$$$. Can you help Ray?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The median of a set of numbers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{2i-1}$$$ is the number $$$c_{i}$$$ where $$$c_{1}, c_{2}, \\ldots, c_{2i-1}$$$ represents $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{2i-1}$$$ sorted in nondecreasing order. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the array $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\leq b_i \\leq 10^9$$$) — the elements of $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed the sum of $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output one line containing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there exists an array $$$a$$$ such that $$$b_i$$$ is the median of $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_{2i-1}$$$ for all $$$i$$$, and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise. The case of letters in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" do not matter (so "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will also be accepted)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n4\n6 2 1 3\n1\n4\n5\n4 -8 5 6 -7\n2\n3 3\n4\n2 1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\nYES\nNO\nYES\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n8\n-8 2 -6 -5 -4 3 3 2\n7\n1 1 3 1 0 -2 -1\n7\n6 12 8 6 2 6 10\n6\n5 1 2 3 6 7\n5\n1 3 4 3 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\nYES\nNO\nNO\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second case of the first sample, the array $$$[4]$$$ will generate an OmkArray of $$$[4]$$$, as the median of the first element is $$$4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth case of the first sample, the array $$$[3, 2, 5]$$$ will generate an OmkArray of $$$[3, 3]$$$, as the median of $$$3$$$ is $$$3$$$ and the median of $$$2, 3, 5$$$ is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fifth case of the first sample, the array $$$[2, 1, 0, 3, 4, 4, 3]$$$ will generate an OmkArray of $$$[2, 1, 2, 3]$$$ as "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$2$$$ is $$$2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$0, 1, 2$$$ is $$$1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$0, 1, 2, 3, 4$$$ is $$$2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" and the median of $$$0, 1, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4$$$ is $$$3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second case of the second sample, the array $$$[1, 0, 4, 3, 5, -2, -2, -2, -4, -3, -4, -1, 5]$$$ will generate an OmkArray of $$$[1, 1, 3, 1, 0, -2, -1]$$$, as "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$1$$$ is $$$1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$0, 1, 4$$$ is $$$1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$0, 1, 3, 4, 5$$$ is $$$3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$-2, -2, 0, 1, 3, 4, 5$$$ is $$$1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$-4, -2, -2, -2, 0, 1, 3, 4, 5$$$ is $$$0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the median of $$$-4, -4, -3, -2, -2, -2, 0, 1, 3, 4, 5$$$ is $$$-2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" and the median of $$$-4, -4, -3, -2, -2, -2, -1, 0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 5$$$ is $$$-1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For all cases where the answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", it can be proven that it is impossible to find an array $$$a$$$ such that $$$b$$$ is the OmkArray of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1536D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1536/problem/D"}